        "title": "Best thing to see in Kathmandu",
        "text": "This is the most interesting and fascinating thing I've seen in Kathmandu. The temple itself you cannot go into but the cremations taking place on the Bagmati River are the highlight. \n\nIt's 1000 rupees to get in (a bit steep compared to other temples, especially as you cannot go in) and I paid another 500 for a guide, but it was well worth having the guide because he gave me so much information I never would of had otherwise. \n\nIt's fascinating to see how another culture handles death and what ceremonies they have for the deceased.\n\nDefinitely worth a visit, especially if you are at Boudha Stupa which is only a short walk away. Both are walk-able from Thamel if you have the time to do so.",
