        "title": "very interesting and educational",
        "text": "on a recent tour we stopped for a half hour  at this site where you see cremations going on. It was most interesting to see how cremations are done and our guide was excellent in explaining the rituals.  I did not find it any sadder then funerals which I go to all the time as I am an organist at a church.  In a lot of ways throwing the ashes in the river makes a lot of sense compared to buying a burial plot with an expensive headstone.\n\nWe also saw some wisemen there.  We were across the river from the cremations so did not interfere with the families or the services.  It was interesting to know that very sick individuals are transported there before they die.  \n\nWe saw other cremations on the Ganges in India but this was the most interesting.",
