      {
        "review_id": 256221412,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r256221412-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "An experience, but blatantly overpriced",
        "text": "The Pashupatinath is one of the most sacred Hindu temples, and for non-Hindus it is definitely an experience. It is full of \"sadhus\" (pilgrims) and worshipping Hindus, and it is also a place of open-air cremation on the banks of a small river. The cremations are public, and crowds of spectators gather readily; this is something which may irritate many \"Westerners\", and I admit that even though I consider myself an open-minded and seasoned traveller I was more shaken up by the spectacle than I had expected, too.\n\nHowever, I was even more shocked by the temple surroundings: it was full of beggars, but also of maimed and visibly sick people. I have read that many Hindus wish to die at the Pashupatinath temple; some people that lay crammed on the ground gave the impression that they were soon going to. Again, this may be an important part of Nepali / Hindu culture, but nevertheless I could not help getting more uneasy than I had expected. In fact, I was so uncomfortable that I completely skipped visiting the main temple.\n\nAll the above points concern my personal, subjective experience and I believe that for other travellers, the place may have a completely opposite effect: the way that the worshipping Hindus deal with death (their own or that of loved ones) in this place may surely appeal to many, and the sadhus and crowds of worshippers give the precincts a buzzing vibe.\n\nHowever, I believe that objectively the entrance fee of 1000 nepalese rupees (about 10 USD!) is far too high. Signs claim that the money goes into the maintenance and renovation of this UN heritage site, but I am not sure how reliable that is in a corrupt country like Nepal. But in any case, I quite frankly did not think that the place was worth that entrance fee as a tourist site.",
        "review_tip": null,
