        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r254782978-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Unique in every aspect!",
        "text": "Visited the Pashupatinath Temple the day before the Sivarati Hindu festival and wow!!!  We had the most incredible visit.  We walked through the temple, saw the public Hindu funeral and cremation, watched the hundreds of Sadhu (holy men) lining the Temple, visited the Elderly Public Assistance Home inside the Temple complex, and visited the Naga Baba (Naked holy-man).  The Naga Baba even invited us onto their platform to sit with them, drinking masala tea and watch their daily actions.  We would recommend coming to Pashupatinath to everyone with a mature mindset!!  Be sure to take a tour also with a guide - it was incredibly helpful to learn all of the intricacies of what was happening.",
